                <pb facs="0553" n="545" sameAs="frus:frus1941v03/pg545"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.79682/34: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Walton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-12-23T15:00:00-00:44">December 23, 1941—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 23—12:42 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>133. Department’s 85, December 20, 6 p.m. President Barclay and I have already
                    discussed subject and Legislature will enact law enabling him to deal
                    effectively with situation along lines suggested by Department.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Walton</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
